abstract: >-
  Modular MATLAB code that solves the nonlinear shallow water (Saint-Venant) equations in one space dimension by finite
  volume methods, over a variable bottom that may emerge from the water, with walls, wave-making, open or periodic ends
  and an optional bottom friction. Each ingredient is chosen in the configuration: sixteen numerical fluxes,
  reconstructions from MUSCL to MP5 with nine slope limiters, explicit integrators or the solvers of MATLAB, boundary and
  initial conditions, bottoms and friction laws. The first-order scheme uses the hydrostatic reconstruction of Audusse
  et al. (2004), and the second-order scheme its extension to reconstructed depths and free surfaces; both keep a lake
  at rest over any bottom, at a shoreline, next to a solid wall and at open or wave-making ends, the open ends letting
  waves out through their Riemann invariants.
